PING(1)                      User Commands

NAME
    ping - send ICMP echo requests

SYNOPSIS
    ping [-c COUNT] [-s SIZE] [-W MILLISECONDS] HOST

DESCRIPTION
    Sends COUNT (default 4) echo requests of SIZE (default 56) payload
    bytes one second apart and prints each reply with its TTL and round
    trip time in milliseconds, then a summary. -W bounds the wait for each
    reply (default 2000 ms). HOST is resolved with the resolver of
    getaddrinfo in netdb.h. Requests go through the echo interface of /dev/net,
    which matches replies to the kernel's own requests; there are no raw
    sockets. Exits 0 when at least one reply arrived.

SEE ALSO
    net(1), nc(1), index(7)
